# Product

Vision Studio is a producer's translator. Describe what you hear, in words, with your voice, or with an instrument, and it makes the sound, explains how it got there, and teaches you to make it yourself in Logic.

Four rooms. Create makes something new. Genre deep dive studies a curated genre and can open Create with those traits. Analyse improves a track, and Tweak reshapes a sample. For the hackathon, Create and Genre deep dive are live. Analyse and Tweak stay marked Soon. There is no level setting. Spec section 11 is the full set of rules.

Create today:

- An agent fills a song brief. Bedrock asks in the producer's own words, one question at a time, up to 5. Facets then branch from the answers, and Go deeper can ask three more. If Bedrock is off or fails, it uses the slot question text, then facet importance order. Never ask a slot the producer or the audio already filled. Never ask a facet twice.
- The composer chooses "A full idea" or "One sound". One sound asks only sound type, genre, duration, mood, and brightness, and returns one layer with three variations.
- Every question offers: an answer, You decide, Skip this, Skip all and build.
- Skip all and build always produces a prompt, however little input is given. The render action is Build.
- Output options for a full idea: drums, chords, bass, melody, texture, all layers separately, full mix.
- Never ask tempo. Derive it from mood and energy, or detect it from audio. A turn or render in flight cannot be sent again. Every turn has a client request id, and a repeat returns the same response. Before a brief is ready, and before every render, missing tempo, bar count, key, and output are filled. A journey is an arc. Structure is only a bar count.
- Each layer returns 3 variations.
- Every result explains how it was made, and how to make it in Logic. MIDI is not shown on its own. Export to Logic lists the MIDI files with the audio.
